### Register - success
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Hana Abdelbari",
  "email": "hana@example.com",
  "phone": "+201001234567",
  "password": "Passw0rd123"
}

### Register - duplicate email (expect 409)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Someone Else",
  "email": "HANA@example.com",
  "password": "Passw0rd123"
}

### Register - invalid data (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "123"
}

### Try to register as admin (role must be ignored)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Sneaky",
  "email": "sneaky@example.com",
  "password": "Passw0rd123",
  "role": "SuperAdmin"
}

### Wrong method (expect 405, not 500)
GET http://localhost:5001/auth/register

### Login (saves the token for the next requests)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "hana@example.com",
  "password": "Passw0rd123"
}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken); %}

### Wrong password (expect 401)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "hana@example.com", "password": "WrongPass1" }

### Unknown email (expect 401, same message)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "nobody@example.com", "password": "Passw0rd123" }

### Me without token (expect 401)
GET http://localhost:5001/users/me

### Me with token (expect 200)
GET http://localhost:5001/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Me with a tampered token (expect 401)
GET http://localhost:5001/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}x

### 1) Login (save refresh token as "r1")
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "hana@example.com", "password": "Passw0rd123" }

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken);
    client.global.set("r1", response.body.refreshToken); %}

### 2) Refresh with r1 (expect 200, save the new one as "r2")
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{r1}}" }

> {% client.global.set("r2", response.body.refreshToken); %}

### 3) Reuse the OLD r1 (expect 401, and the whole session gets revoked)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{r1}}" }

### 4) Now even r2 must be dead (expect 401)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{r2}}" }

### 5) Garbage token (expect 401)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "abc" }

### 6) Missing field (expect 400 bad request)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 7) Logout (expect 204)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{r1}}" }

### 8) Refresh after logout (expect 401)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{r1}}" }

### 9) Logout all without token (expect 401)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/logout-all

### 10) Logout all with token (expect 204)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/logout-all
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
